.TH DEEPIN-LIFERAFT 1 "July 2026" "deepin-liferaft 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deepin-liferaft \- monitor memory pressure and present a force-quit dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deepin-liferaft
.RI [ --hidden ]
.br
.B deepin-liferaft --self-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deepin-liferaft
monitors the current systemd user cgroup for Fedora-style systemd-oomd memory pressure and swap conditions.
When pressure remains unsafe, it freezes selected DDE application cgroups and opens a macOS-style dialog that can resume or force quit them.
.PP
Closing the dialog, stopping the service, or sending SIGTERM or SIGINT thaws every cgroup frozen by this process before exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --hidden
Run the pressure monitor without showing the dialog at startup. This is the mode used by the systemd user service.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run built-in policy, parsing, formatting, and freezer ownership checks, then exit with status zero on success.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/deepin-liferaft.service
Systemd user service that starts the monitor with
.BR --hidden .
.TP
.I /sys/fs/cgroup/user.slice/user-UID.slice/user@UID.service/
User cgroup from which memory pressure, reclaim, memory, and swap data are read.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
request a clean shutdown. Owned frozen cgroups are thawed before the process exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-oomd (8),
.BR systemd.resource-control (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Ston Jia <ston.jia@outlook.com>
